  "lines": {
    "hook": "What happens if you live in space?",
    "d1": "Day one. Fluids drift up to your head, so your face puffs up and your legs get skinny.",
    "d2": "Day two. Your inner ear can't tell which way is down, so you feel sick.",
    "w2": "Week two. Your spine stretches out, and you grow up to two inches taller.",
    "m1": "Month one. Your bones get weaker, losing about one percent every month.",
    "m3": "Month three. Your muscles shrink, so you have to work out two hours a day.",
    "m6": "Month six. The back of your eyes can flatten, and your vision gets blurry.",
    "end": "Back on Earth, you can barely stand. Would you still go?"
  },
